@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium requirement graph — derive chain, satisfy to blocks, verify to test cases.
'   usecase:      Operational -> functional derive chain with full coverage.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       systems-engineering
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Requirement - Medium Graph

' Layers: operational requirements drive functional requirements, which are
' satisfied by blocks and verified by test cases. «deriveReqt» edges flow
' top-down from operational to functional.

' ---- Operational requirements -------------------------------------------
class "Op: Continuous Operation" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-O1
  text : "The system shall operate 24/7 without unscheduled downtime."
}

class "Op: Remote Monitoring" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-O2
  text : "Operators shall monitor the system remotely."
}

' ---- Functional requirements (derived) -----------------------------------
class "Fn: Auto Restart" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-F1
  text : "Software shall restart critical services within 30 s of failure."
}

class "Fn: Telemetry Stream" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-F2
  text : "Software shall publish metrics at 1 Hz to the dashboard."
}

class "Fn: Alert Pipeline" <<requirement>> {
  id : REQ-F3
  text : "Software shall page on-call within 60 s of an SLO breach."
}

' ---- Blocks --------------------------------------------------------------
class "SupervisorProcess" <<block>>
class "MetricsExporter" <<block>>
class "AlertRouter" <<block>>

' ---- Test cases ----------------------------------------------------------
class "RestartBench" <<testCase>> { id : TC-101 }
class "TelemetryCheck" <<testCase>> { id : TC-102 }
class "AlertDrill" <<testCase>> { id : TC-103 }

' ---- Derive chain: operational -> functional ----------------------------
"Fn: Auto Restart" ..> "Op: Continuous Operation" : <<deriveReqt>>
"Fn: Telemetry Stream" ..> "Op: Remote Monitoring" : <<deriveReqt>>
"Fn: Alert Pipeline" ..> "Op: Remote Monitoring" : <<deriveReqt>>

' ---- Satisfaction: blocks satisfy functional ----------------------------
"SupervisorProcess" ..> "Fn: Auto Restart" : <<satisfy>>
"MetricsExporter" ..> "Fn: Telemetry Stream" : <<satisfy>>
"AlertRouter" ..> "Fn: Alert Pipeline" : <<satisfy>>

' ---- Verification: tests verify functional ------------------------------
"RestartBench" ..> "Fn: Auto Restart" : <<verify>>
"TelemetryCheck" ..> "Fn: Telemetry Stream" : <<verify>>
"AlertDrill" ..> "Fn: Alert Pipeline" : <<verify>>

note bottom of "Op: Continuous Operation"
  <b>Edge stereotypes recap:</b>
  «deriveReqt» — child derived from parent
  «satisfy»    — design/block fulfills req
  «verify»     — test case proves req
  «trace»      — generic link
end note

@enduml
